Gear can now be moved onto a different slot.

1) FORGE REFIT <item> <slot> for metal, SEW REFIT <item> <slot> for cloth.
   - A bracer becomes a greave, a cap becomes a collar.
   - The body it was cut for does not change: a gnome's bracer becomes a
     gnome's greave.

2) The armor it offers is conserved across the move.
   - A slot that carries more of a suit's protection needs a lower level to
     offer the same defence, so a piece keeps what it was worth.
   - Packing a large piece into a small slot loses whatever will not fit.
     It does not concentrate.

3) Material is accounted for as it is when resizing.
   - Growing into a larger slot needs a bar or bolt for the difference.
   - Shrinking into a smaller one leaves an offcut carrying the stats.

See HELP FORGE and HELP SEW.
